=== p2-windows · W7 · page:system/DataRepair (WinUI 3 / Fluent) ===
Parity unit : page:system/DataRepair   kind=page   web route=/data-repair
Web source  : web/src/features/system/pages/DataRepairPage.tsx
ADR refs    : ADR-002, ADR-004, ADR-005, ADR-006, ADR-011, ADR-013, ADR-014, ADR-015
Runner      : .NET 10.0.300 SDK present (dotnet --version 10.0.300), maui-windows workload — NOT blocked.

=== APPROACH ===
- The repository's WinUI app is code-first C# (no .xaml page files); every feature surface lives under
  apps/windows/TeslaSync.App/feature-views/<Name>/ as <Name>.Model.cs + <Name>.Projection.cs (pure,
  Microsoft.UI-free projection, unit-tested headlessly), <Name>.Source.cs (generated-client feed, ADR-004),
  <Name>.ViewModel.cs (INotifyPropertyChanged + IDisposable observable state holder) and <Name>.cs (the Fluent
  view). The generated prompt's idealized "DataRepairPage.xaml + DataRepairPageViewModel.cs under
  TeslaSync/Features/System" is mapped onto these real conventions (same mapping as every shipped W7 page, e.g.
  DataExportPage); the surface registers itself with the W4 ShellPageFactory by route name ("DataRepair").
- Namespace: the page lives in TeslaSync.App.FeatureViews.SystemOps (NOT ".System" — a ".System" leaf shadows the
  global System namespace). RouteTable already maps Page("DataRepair","data-repair",RouteGroup.SystemOps,
  "Data Repair","\uE90F"), so the registered route name is exact.
- Data sources bound to the generated C# client (ADR-004) through DataRepairClientFeed in DataRepairPage.Source.cs.
  The manifest classes this page as "local state", but the web page does fetch + mutate, so the feed binds the seven
  generated operations verified in apps/windows/Generated/Api/ApiEndpoints.cs:
    useQuery(['stale-sessions']) -> GET    /data-repair/stale-sessions       (get_api_v1_data_repair_stale_sessions)
    charging updateMut           -> PUT    /data-repair/charging/{id}         (put_api_v1_data_repair_charging_id)
    charging closeMut            -> POST   /data-repair/charging/{id}/close   (post_api_v1_data_repair_charging_id_close)
    charging discardMut          -> DELETE /data-repair/charging/{id}         (delete_api_v1_data_repair_charging_id)
    drive updateMut              -> PUT    /data-repair/drive/{id}            (put_api_v1_data_repair_drive_id)
    drive closeMut               -> POST   /data-repair/drive/{id}/close      (post_api_v1_data_repair_drive_id_close)
    drive discardMut             -> DELETE /data-repair/drive/{id}            (delete_api_v1_data_repair_drive_id)
  The default EmptyDataRepairFeed resolves the empty state (the shell uses the parameterless ctor); the view-model is
  exercised in tests with a FakeDataRepairFeed driving the loading/empty/error/success matrix and the six mutations.
- The opt-in AI repair suggestions panel (web AIDataRepairSuggestions, withAiFeature) is a SEPARATE parity unit and is
  intentionally out of scope here (it is not among the 8 manifest panels); the deterministic stale-session list + per-row
  edit forms are the canonical baseline reproduced natively.
- SI: the page carries no display-boundary unit conversion — the web admin tool shows raw stored values and labels them
  verbatim ("Distance (m)"/"Duration (s)"/"Max Speed (m/s)" are SI; "Energy Added (kWh)"/"Charger Power (kW)"/
  "Duration (min)" are the web's literal field labels), so the native port matches them 1:1 (DataRepairProjection /
  DataRepairRegistration.NumberField/Percent). Battery % and counts flow through invariant formatting; "hours open" and
  the row timestamp are ported from the web hoursOpen/formatDateTime helpers.
- Strings: every visible literal resolves through ILocalizer with the exact web t() key + English fallback
  (DataRepairStrings.Resolve), the established windows convention; the page renders correct English via key-fallback.

